+- **arXiv:2512.10858 - "Scaling Behavior of Discrete Diffusion Language Models" (submitted 2025-12-11; last revised 2026-02-15; arXiv resolved):** Track: EDLM operator-seed. Studies scaling laws for discrete diffusion language models and reports a 10B-parameter uniform-diffusion model trained for 10^22 FLOPs while narrowing the likelihood gap at scale. Scaling precondition for the EDLM operator seed: discrete diffusion is a foundation-model substrate with scale behavior, not merely a small-model generator novelty. Model size, FLOP, and scaling-law claims are source-reported only.
+- **arXiv:2605.26106 - "Looped Diffusion Language Models" (submitted 2026-05-25; arXiv resolved):** Track: EDLM operator-seed. Loops early-middle masked-diffusion transformer layers and reports up to 3.3x fewer training FLOPs for matched performance plus up to 8.5 GSM8K points from the looped design. Compute-scaling follow-up for EDLM: recurrent depth and adaptive loop counts give an operator-seed route for test-time compute in masked diffusion without self-seeding the paradigm. Training-FLOP and reasoning-benchmark gains are source-reported only.
+- **arXiv:2603.13243 - "Think First, Diffuse Fast: Improving Diffusion Language Model Reasoning via Autoregressive Plan Conditioning" (submitted 2026-02-20; arXiv resolved):** Track: EDLM operator-seed. Prepends an autoregressive natural-language plan to a diffusion LM and reports large reasoning/code gains with stable diffusion inference across seeds. Operator-seed design hint for EDLM: use an external plan or verifier as globally visible conditioning rather than asking the diffusion model to discover the full reasoning scaffold alone. Accuracy, latency, and stability figures are source-reported only.
